 # Weight-PDF Conversion
-
-
 ## Overview
-Weight-PDF Conversion transforms a vector of discrete weights that sum to 1 into a probability density function (PDF) that integrates to 1 over given spatial or temporal intervals, and vice versa [S1, S2, unofficial]. This method serves as the inverse operation to CDF Integration from Weights, bridging the gap between discrete sampling weights and continuous density representations required for accurate volume rendering classification [S1, S2, unofficial]. It is distinct from simple normalization by accounting for the variable width of the intervals defined by the boundaries $t$ [S2, unofficial].
