 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Multivariate Conditional Weighting
-This variant extends weight-PDF conversion to multivariate scenarios where variables are dependent. It distinguishes between "guiding variables" (which define the interval of interest, e.g., cloud density) and "following variables" (which are important only when guiding variables are within a specific interval, e.g., vertical velocity) [S3]. For following variables, the weighting function is constructed using the conditional probability density function (PDF) of the following variable given that the guiding variable lies within a specific interval $[B_0, B_1]$ [S3]. This approach assigns increased weight where the conditional PDF is high, reducing the relative importance of values outside the guiding variable's interval of interest [S3]. Quality improves with narrower intervals, similar to univariate cases [S3].
